{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/4757-thoughts-on-kickstarter-and-print-on-demand","id":4757,"title":"Thoughts on kickstarter and print-on-demand","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-06T18:09:40-08:00","id":4757,"title":"Thoughts on kickstarter and print-on-demand","content":"Maybe someone else is interested in sharing some thoughts on this topic?<br /> I\u00b4m glad the industry managed to find new ways in financing and distributing our beloved games. Seems to me the rpg-industry made it much, much better than music/entertainment-industry.<br /> Some things realy bother me:<br /> I\u00b4m from germany, where p&amp;p gaming is still alive and kicking. Maybe even more than ten years ago.<br /> The more time i spend watching stuff like kickstarter/crowdfunding and print on demand grow, the more it frustrates me.<br /> Why?<br /> Kickstarter has no real PayPal support (no direct) and most of the people over here in europe don\u00b4t have credit cards like in the US. And the young gamer\u00b4s parents, too.<br /> Print on demand can be a great thing and i realy support it but then again this is something that i just can\u00b4t afford in most cases (with shipping from the US to europe....)<br /> Just got the feeling that the great stuff evolving in the US won\u00b4t ever really make it in europe.<br /> I\u00b4m not talking about translations but the whole thing seems more and more be separated by creditcard yes/no and the big ocean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/709-nihil","name":"Nihil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar709_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T22:12:42-08:00","id":4855,"title":"","content":"I would love to see businesses like DriveThruRPG set things up abroad so that other countries' gamers can reliably get the books they would happily buy if it wasn't for the horrific long-distance shipping costs. And it would be amazing to have more games from abroad translated and made similarly available in the states. As for Kickstarter, I don't know why they wouldn't take Paypal. That's got to be quite frustrating. Have you contacted them about it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T22:57:28-08:00","id":4870,"title":"","content":"While I'll agree that credit cards can be an issue, I know that the company drive-thru uses for printing has at least one european printing center. They just route the job to wherever it makes the most sense/that has the capacity.<br /> <br /> And actually on the topic of credit cards, I know there are european based disposable credit cards available, I've had to deal with them. Failing that, I don't know what services the banks offer, but I know one of the ones that I have through mine is the ability to set up a single-use temporary visa number. I get it, set a limit on how much can go through it, use it, and tell the bank to get rid of the number when I'm done. The money comes straight out of my account.<br /> <br /> Lastly on kickstarter, I know there are some kickstarters that have support for paypal, however I suspect there are additional high fees for doing so. One of the big headaches with kickstarter is getting the numbers predictable. If you don't know how much of a percentage you are losing to processing fees on any given transaction, you can't really set a price. Well, you can but you end up having to make it the higher price just to ensure it's covered, which might push the cost of the product higher decreasing sales. Balancing act unfortunately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T06:03:17-08:00","id":5005,"title":"","content":"These horrendous shipping costs people talk about, have anyone ever <i>experienced</i> those?<br /> <br /> Because according to the test I just made, I can get WoD: Slashers shipped in 8 days for $5. And I live in Europe.<br /> <br /> The thing is, DrivethruRPG doesn't just print everything in the US and sends it off across the atlantic ocean. They have printers in several parts of the world to specifically eliminate the shipping cost problem. There's a DTRPG printer in the UK, for instance, so anyone in Europe would pay virtually nothing for shipping. So are you <i>actually</i> experiencing high shipping costs, or are you just assuming that because DTRPG is an American company?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/508-sikker","name":"sikker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T06:23:32-08:00","id":5018,"title":"","content":"I believe the most I was ever charged in the concept of shipping was around 2-3 bucks. And at most I wait 2 weeks for my books, wich is exactly I am told they could take. Of course I figure they were all printed in the UK and sending from there to Spain shouldn't cost much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T07:44:38-08:00","id":5065,"title":"","content":"I just sent a comp copy of a sourcebook to an artist in Portugal. Cost me less than 10USD all told (well, I mean, I get the book at cost, so if I'd paid full price it would have been more, but my point is shipping was only about 7USD). POD to Europe is pretty reasonably shipped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T09:51:29-08:00","id":5164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sikker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/4757-thoughts-on-kickstarter-and-print-on-demand?p=5005#post5005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These horrendous shipping costs people talk about, have anyone ever <i>experienced</i> those?</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, I haven't heard about shipping costs lately. I think my impression of this is out of date. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T12:22:18-08:00","id":5307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KismetRose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/4757-thoughts-on-kickstarter-and-print-on-demand?p=5164#post5164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit, I haven't heard about shipping costs lately. I think my impression of this is out of date. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There has been a sizeable uptick in issues dealing with shipping from Kickstarter lately. changes with the various shipping organizations have drastically increased US-&gt;International shipping costs, resulting in a lot of difficulties. But that's kickstarter, not Drive-Thru. I know there was an incident reported on the rpg.net forums about a month ago on the topic, but that was more a case of mis-management combined with UPS charging excessive additional fees to the recipients of packages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T12:50:27-08:00","id":5333,"title":"","content":"On the absolute minimum, most PDF sources also allow you to print your PDF. It's not the same as having a book, but digital tech certainly makes it much easier for games to cross international borders.<br /> <br /> As far as KS goes, it is not a great venue for international sales. That seems to be by design by KS (all KS drives have to be US or UK based somehow) and their choice to restrict pledging to an Amazon based system.<br /> <br /> POD is better for international sales because, as mentioned, a POD service can have printers in multiple countries to reduce shipping costs.<br /> <br /> In general though, international shipping is a pain in the ass. There's a huge morass of issues to navigate and lots of things that cause dissonance between seller and buyer. If the shipper has to handle import fees and/or taxes, rather than charge the seller more for shipping, they charge the buyer a COD fee to get their books. The RPG.net thread was focused on this (and this is not a company specific issue, all the big international shippers do it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T10:31:57-08:00","id":7450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/4757-thoughts-on-kickstarter-and-print-on-demand#post4757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe someone else is interested in sharing some thoughts on this topic?<br /> I\u00b4m glad the industry managed to find new ways in financing and distributing our beloved games. Seems to me the rpg-industry made it much, much better than music/entertainment-industry.<br /> Some things realy bother me:<br /> I\u00b4m from germany, where p&amp;p gaming is still alive and kicking. Maybe even more than ten years ago.<br /> The more time i spend watching stuff like kickstarter/crowdfunding and print on demand grow, the more it frustrates me.<br /> Why?<br /> Kickstarter has no real PayPal support (no direct) and most of the people over here in europe don\u00b4t have credit cards like in the US. And the young gamer\u00b4s parents, too.<br /> Print on demand can be a great thing and i realy support it but then again this is something that i just can\u00b4t afford in most cases (with shipping from the US to europe....)<br /> Just got the feeling that the great stuff evolving in the US won\u00b4t ever really make it in europe.<br /> I\u00b4m not talking about translations but the whole thing seems more and more be separated by creditcard yes/no and the big ocean.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'm also from Germany I would dispute the points you've made: <br /> <br /> Credit Card - this stopped to be an issue some time ago. Unless you are a customer at the largest and most primitive bank in Germany (the one starting with an &quot;S&quot;), you can get yourself a pre-paid Credit Card. I'm squarely in the low income demographic and can afford one (its around 25\u20ac a year).<br /> <br /> Print on Demand - I only know about DTRPG and they have a printer in the UK, so shipping isn't an issue.<br /> <br /> Sure it sucks that we have to jump over a few more hoops, but in the end we are all better off than say people in South America or Africa. Last time I checked sending anything there was horrendously expensive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To a player who wanted his character to attend a very &quot;special&quot; school:<br /> There is no Charles F. Lupus school for gifted werewolves.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/971-arag","name":"Arag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar971_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}